(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase460SchemeAlignmentAndRacketConcepts"
  :createdAt 1789240000000
  :status "planned"
  :priorityOrder 1
  :summary "Scheme Alignment and Racket Concepts: stop being gratuitously different from the Lisp the model already knows, adopt Racket designs for the module system, located syntax and blame-carrying contracts, and keep Racket out of the deployed runtime."
  :phase "Phase460SchemeAlignmentAndRacketConcepts"
  :baseline "Measured 2026-09-12 under cl100k over 888 files and 1512691 tokens. Seven of eleven divergent core forms save exactly zero tokens by being abbreviated, covering 16041 uses: df and define are both one token, as are dfs and struct, mt and match, do and begin, x and provide, i and require, f and field. The remaining renames are also free: fn to lambda, str to string, nil to null, all zero delta across a further 5576 uses; dfe to enum saves 165 tokens. ASL already shares if 3011, let 5263, and 1214, or 1265, not 1530, cond 393, case, quote and lambda with Scheme. The binding form costs the same in both shapes: ASL (let [(a 1) (b 2)] body) and Racket (let ([a 1] [b 2]) body) are 13 tokens each. The definition form is at parity with its Racket equivalent carrying the same information: ASL 19 tokens against define/contract 18 and Typed Racket 20. Converting true and false to hash-t and hash-f would cost 0.43 percent and is rejected."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task46001"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-460"
      :title "Rename the core forms to their Scheme spellings, at zero token cost"
      :kind :language
      :state :completed
      :lane "alignment"
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789240000000
      :updatedAt 1789424300000
      :motivation "A byte pair tokenizer assigns a single token to define, struct, match, begin, provide, require, lambda and string precisely because those words are frequent in the code it was trained on, and that same frequency is what gives a model its prior. Abbreviating them therefore loses the prior and saves nothing: measured, the abbreviation is worth zero tokens across 21617 uses. The present surface is the worst available position, a language that looks like a Lisp so the model predicts Lisp forms, while every form is renamed so the predictions are wrong. Correcting it is free."
      :purpose "The core forms carry their Scheme and Racket spellings wherever the spelling is measured at one token: define, struct, enum, lambda, match, begin, provide, require, field, string, null. try is retained against with-handlers, which measures three tokens: a rename that raises cost is refused even when it improves family consistency, because measured token count decides and pattern does not. The abbreviated spellings are removed rather than aliased. true and false stay as they are, being valid Racket bindings and cheaper than the hash forms. The abbreviated family is not uniform today: df and dfs are one token while dfl, dfn and dfe are two, splitting as d plus fl, df plus n and d plus fe. Every corresponding full word is one token: define, struct, enum, lambda, list, name, type, proc. A uniformly single-token and uniformly transparent family is therefore available at the full words. A uniformly two-word family is also consistent and costs two to three tokens per use, define-function at two and define-struct at three, which on the 6881 uses of df is 0.45 percent of the corpus; it is recorded as the priced alternative rather than adopted. The docstring keyword stays, being one token against two for any comment form."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Eleven core forms renamed, old spellings removed" "Measured cost recomputed on the tree and recorded" "true, false and the docstring keyword retained with the measurement that justifies each"]
      :owns ["asl/grammar/language-semantics.asn" "asl/grammar/grammar.asn" "asl/tools/engine_js.h" "asl/packages" "harness/src" "intel/src" "mem/src" "agent-core/src"]
      :targetSymbols ["df" "dfs" "dfe" "fn" "mt" "do"]
      :relatedSymbols ["names" "semantics" "foreign"]
      :invariants ["D51" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task45901"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46001"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46001.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["An abbreviated spelling fails rather than resolving through an alias." "Executed assertion count is unchanged across the rename, so nothing was silently unbound." "The recomputed token total moves by less than one tenth of a percent, confirming the rename was free rather than assumed free." "A spelling inside a string literal is not rewritten."]
      :gateReadiness :verified
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46001" :status :baselineVerified :contract D81Baseline :exitCode 1 :failure "language-semantics.asn must define schemeCoreFormsAlignment semantic")
      :historicalReceipts ["rc-task46001-verified-20260912"]
      :reviewStatus :approved
      :actionDag ["Fix the mapping." "Rewrite mechanically in one pass with the CamelCase conversion." "Recompute and record." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 4
      :receipts ["rc-task46001-verified-20260912"])
    (:task
      :id "Task46002"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-460"
      :title "Adopt the Racket binding shape and decline the cheaper Clojure one"
      :kind :language
      :state :completed
      :lane "alignment"
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789240000000
      :updatedAt 1789424500000
      :motivation "The current binding form is a third shape belonging to no existing Lisp: ASL writes (let [(a 1) (b 2)] body) where Racket writes (let ([a 1] [b 2]) body) and Clojure writes (let [a 1 b 2] body). Measured, ASL and Racket cost 13 tokens and Clojure costs 11. The cheaper form would save 0.69 percent across 5249 uses, and taking it would place the language a third distance from both references, which is the condition that produced the present problem. Alignment with one reference is worth more than two tokens a binding."
      :purpose "The binding form is Racket's. The choice, including the rejected Clojure option and the 0.69 percent it would have saved, is recorded so it is not reopened as an efficiency idea."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Binding form matches Racket exactly" "The rejected cheaper option recorded with its measured value" "One reference dialect, not a blend"]
      :owns ["asl/grammar/language-semantics.asn" "asl/tools/engine_js.h" "asl/packages" "harness/src"]
      :targetSymbols ["let"]
      :relatedSymbols ["names" "semantics"]
      :invariants ["D51" "D81"]
